---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Web emulation model"
  description="How December Reach acquires real OS source and performs emulation in a JavaScript backend."
  current="emulation"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">04 / WEB EMULATION</p>
    <h1>The web is the way in.<br /><span>Not the machine.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">
      December Reach uses the website to acquire and preload OS source. The
      actual emulation work belongs to the JavaScript backend, not to a
      browser-side CPU simulator.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="section-index">EXECUTION PATH</p>
        <h2>Three distinct responsibilities.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Source preparation, system execution and web access are separate
        responsibilities. Keeping that boundary clear prevents the frontend
        from becoming a pretend emulator.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="emulation-flow">
      <article class="emulation-step">
        <span class="emulation-number">01</span>
        <span class="emulation-label">FRONTEND</span>
        <h2>Source acquisition</h2>
        <p>The site obtains the operating-system source and preloads what is needed before an emulation session begins.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="emulation-step">
        <span class="emulation-number">02</span>
        <span class="emulation-label">BACKEND</span>
        <h2>JavaScript emulation</h2>
        <p>The backend owns the emulation process and execution environment. CPU, memory and device behavior are not simulated by the website UI.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="emulation-step">
        <span class="emulation-number">03</span>
        <span class="emulation-label">WEB ACCESS</span>
        <h2>Reach the session</h2>
        <p>The browser is the access surface for the system. It is not the guest machine's execution host.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section">
    <header class="doc-label">
      <span class="doc-number">01</span>
      <h2>Why the split matters</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="doc-content">
      <p>The frontend and emulator are not interchangeable layers. The frontend is responsible for obtaining and preparing source. The JavaScript backend performs the emulation itself.</p>
      <p>This keeps the guest operating system's execution model out of presentation code and allows the emulation runtime to evolve independently from the website interface.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section">
    <header class="doc-label">
      <span class="doc-number">02</span>
      <h2>Source repository</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="doc-content">
      <p>The OS source collection is maintained separately from this website.</p>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/DecemberReach/reach-to-be-reached" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open reach-to-be-reached on GitHub ↗</a></p>
      <div class="callout">This repository contains the static Astro website. The JavaScript emulation service is a separate execution component and is not bundled into the GitHub Pages frontend.</div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
